  "explanation": {
    "md_es": [
      "**There is** (there's) + singular → *There's a sofa.*",
      "**There are** + plural → *There are two chairs.*",
      "",
      "| | Singular | Plural |",
      "|---|---|---|",
      "| + | There is a lamp. | There are two lamps. |",
      "| − | There isn't a lamp. | There aren't any lamps. |",
      "| ? | Is there a lamp? | Are there any lamps? |",
      "",
      "**Respuestas cortas:** *Yes, there is. / No, there isn't. · Yes, there are. / No, there aren't.*",
      "",
      "En español 'hay' es un solo verbo; en inglés **no se omite there** y **no se usa *have***: *There are two bedrooms* (no *Have two bedrooms*)."
    ],
    "common_mistakes_es": [
      {
        "wrong": "In my flat have two bedrooms.",
        "right": "There are two bedrooms in my flat.",
        "note": "'Hay' = there is / there are, no 'have'."
      },
      {
        "wrong": "There is two chairs.",
        "right": "There are two chairs.",
        "note": "Con plural, there are."
      }
    ],
    "false_friends": []
  },
